{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"","title":"Executive Summary","text":""},{"location":"#problem-statement","title":"Problem Statement","text":"<p>Briefly describe the context of the project and the specific problem you are trying to solve.</p>"},{"location":"#objectives","title":"Objectives","text":"<ul> <li>Objective 1</li> <li>Objective 2</li> </ul>"},{"location":"#key-findings-results","title":"Key Findings &amp; Results","text":"<p>Provide a high-level overview of the most important results achieved. Detailed experiment logs should be documented in the Experiments section.</p> <p>[!tip] Quick Link For instructions on reproducing these results, see Setup &amp; Codebase.</p>"},{"location":"methodology/","title":"Methodology","text":""},{"location":"methodology/#theoretical-background","title":"Theoretical Background","text":"<p>Describe the theoretical models or algorithms used in this project. MkDocs supports LaTeX for equations using MathJax:</p> \\[ E = mc^2 \\]"},{"location":"methodology/#data-processing","title":"Data Processing","text":"<p>Explain how the data is acquired, cleaned, and transformed before being fed into the models.</p>"},{"location":"methodology/#experimental-design","title":"Experimental Design","text":"<p>Describe the approach taken to validate the hypotheses, the metrics used, and the baseline models.</p>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/","title":"Setup &amp; Codebase","text":""},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#overview","title":"Overview","text":"<p>The primary codebase is located in the <code>motion-capture</code> repository. It contains the following core components: - <code>easymocap</code>: The core python module for multi-view capture and processing. - <code>apps</code>: Various pipeline applications like calibration, annotation, and reconstruction. - <code>scripts</code>: Helper scripts for preprocessing, postprocessing, and Slurm cluster submissions. - <code>config</code>: Configuration yaml files for the pipelines.</p>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#environment-hpc-setup","title":"Environment &amp; HPC Setup","text":"<p>This project was largely executed on the Digital Research Alliance of Canada (Alliance) cluster.  Key notes from the <code>drac-harness</code> wiki: - Use <code>module load python</code> and standard virtual environments (<code>venv</code>) for python dependencies. - Beware of Slurm gotchas when requesting GPUs (e.g., specifying the exact memory and GPU type). - Custom CUDA extensions might require careful Wheelhouse configurations.</p>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#running-the-pipeline","title":"Running the Pipeline","text":"<p>To run a general motion-capture pipeline, refer to the scripts in <code>motion-capture/scripts/</code> or submit a job via <code>motion-capture/scripts/slurm/</code>.</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/","title":"Ablation: K Contiguous","text":"<p>This section documents the ablation studies for this group.</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#overall-results-plot","title":"Overall Results Plot","text":""},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125","title":"ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125","text":"<ul> <li>Path: <code>cow-2026-07-29/ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125</code></li> <li>Objective: Test performance for configuration <code>ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125</code>.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#results-summary","title":"Results Summary","text":"<p>(Results to be populated from logs)</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940","title":"ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940","text":"<ul> <li>Path: <code>cow-2026-07-29/ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940</code></li> <li>Objective: Test performance for configuration <code>ablation_k3_contiguous_frame194